  "title": "The Saturday Selection, Vol. 127",
  "summary": "Legendary LIFE covers, Orna on interviewing, defectors, and much more.",
  "content": "<p><em>Every day, WITI’s group chats buzz with fresh links. As part of our Saturday send for paid readers, we round up 11 of the best.</em></p><p><em>It’s WITI, on the weekend</em><strong>.</strong></p><div><figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!n2lQ!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe5aaffa9-d0c9-4689-bc75-0254f223717c_838x1024.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!n2lQ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe5aaffa9-d0c9-4689-bc75-0254f223717c_838x1024.jpeg\" width=\"838\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"\" title=\"\"><div><div></div></div></div></a><figcaption>via <a href=\"https://disleelandia.blog/2022/04/30/life-magazine-from-oct-1971-disney-world-opens/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Disleelandia</a></figcaption></figure></div><p><strong>Why are these interesting?</strong></p><p><a href=\"https://www.domestika.org/en/blog/12724-10-legendary-covers-of-life-magazine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">10 Legendary Covers of LIFE Magazine</a> (<em>Domestika</em>)</p><p>After the <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/28/business/media/life-magazine-karlie-kloss.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">exciting relaunch</a>, I wanted to go back in time a bit.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/cmo-today/where-have-all-the-car-commercials-gone-6844790f?mod=author_content_page_1_pos_1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Where Have All the Car Commercials Gone?</a> (<em>WSJ</em>)</p><p>Automakers are emphasizing streaming and regional TV over the big brand storytelling that long dominated prime time.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.nybooks.com/online/2026/08/04/listening-for-the-unconscious-orna-guralnik/?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Listening for the Unconscious</a> (<em>NYRB</em>)</p><p>Orna Guralnik and Merve Emre on the overlap being a great therapist and a great interviewer.</p>\n      <p>\n          <a href=\"https://whyisthisinteresting.substack.com/p/the-saturday-selection-vol-127\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
